<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Polish–Swedish War (1600–1611)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1600">1600</a>–<a href="/years/1611">1611</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Polish–Swedish War of 1600–1611 was fought between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish–Lithuanian Commonwealth</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>, mainly over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonia">Livonia</a>, and grew out of the dynastic quarrel between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sigismund-iii-vasa">Sigismund III Vasa</a> and his uncle Charles IX of Sweden. Sweden invaded Livonia in 1600, but the Commonwealth won major victories, above all Jan Karol Chodkiewicz's at Kircholm in 1605. A truce in 1611 left the situation largely unchanged.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/polish-swedish-war-1600-1611.jpg" alt="Polish–Swedish War (1600–1611)" width="320" height="193" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Peter Snayers · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pieter_Snayers_-_Battle_of_Kircholm,_1605.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
